## Directory Map

What each directory holds, and who owns it:

- `cmd/` — mixed. `main.go` and `custom_routes.go` are user-owned; the
  `generated_*.go` files are the generator's.
- `service/<name>/` — mixed. `service.go` is user-owned; `generated_repos.go`
  is the generator's.
- `endpoint/<name>/` — mixed. `custom_chain.go` is user-owned; `endpoints.go`
  and `generated_chain.go` are the generator's.
- `model/` (model output) — mixed. `<model>.go`, the GORM lifecycle hooks, is
  user-owned; `generated_<model>.go` is the generator's.
- `config/` (config output) — mixed. `config.yaml` and `custom.go` are
  user-owned; `config.go`, `local.go`, `env.go`, `remote.go`, and `loader.go`
  are the generator's.
- `transport/<name>/` — generator-owned. The HTTP and gRPC handlers.
- `client/<name>/` — generator-owned. The generated client demo.
- `sdk/` — generator-owned. The Go SDK (`<name>sdk/`) and, with contract
  output, the TypeScript SDK (`typescript/`).
- `pb/<name>/` (gRPC output) — generator-owned. The proto contracts.
- `repository/` (model output) — generator-owned. The repositories and their
  base.
- `test/` — generator-owned. Generated service tests; put your own tests
  elsewhere.
- `docs/` (contract output) — generator-owned. The OpenAPI and JSON Schema
  contracts.
- `.microgen/` — generator-owned. The project manifest, which enumerates every
  generator-owned artifact.
- `.ai/` — generator-owned. This guide.

## File Ownership

Any file answers two machine-checkable questions:

1. Does its name start with `generated_`? It is rewritten on every generation
   run.
2. Does its first line read `// Code generated by microgen. DO NOT EDIT.`
   (the standard Go generated-code marker)? It is rewritten on every
   generation run.

A file answering yes to either is generator-owned. A file answering no to both
was written once when the project was created and never touched again — it is
yours, unconditionally.

User-owned (safe to edit):

- `cmd/main.go` — startup and shutdown wiring
- `cmd/custom_routes.go` — custom HTTP routes
- `service/<name>/service.go` — business logic
- `endpoint/<name>/custom_chain.go` — custom middleware hooks
- `model/<model>.go` — GORM lifecycle hooks
{{- if .WithConfig }}
- `config/config.yaml` and `config/custom.go` — configuration
{{- end }}
- `README.md` — project documentation

Generator-owned (do not hand-edit; use `microgen extend`):

- `.microgen/manifest.json` — project identity and artifact contract
- `.ai/PROJECT_GUIDE.md` — this guide
- `cmd/generated_*.go` — runtime, service wiring, and route registration
{{- if .WithInteraction }}
- `cmd/generated_interaction.go` — the MCP endpoint wiring
{{- end }}
- `endpoint/<name>/endpoints.go` and `generated_chain.go`
- `service/<name>/generated_repos.go` (model output)
- `model/generated_*.go` and all of `repository/` (model output)
- `transport/<name>/` — HTTP and gRPC handlers
- `client/<name>/demo.go` and `sdk/<name>sdk/`
{{- if .WithGRPC }}
- `pb/<name>/` — proto contracts
{{- end }}
