## API Discovery Protocol

Work in this order, and never guess at a generated name:

1. **Read this guide first**, then the project `README.md` and the generated
   `docs` package.
2. **Godoc is the API reference.** Generated declarations carry their contracts
   as doc comments; `go doc ./model` and `go doc ./endpoint/<name>` answer most
   questions without opening the files.
3. **Never hand-edit generator-owned files**, and never grep or read generated
   source to discover an API this guide and godoc do not show. When the model
   itself must change, run `microgen extend -check -out .` and extend the model.
4. **If the generated API does not expose the operation you need**, stop that
   path and report `MICROGEN_API_GAP` with the language, the service, the
   missing operation, and the compiler diagnostic. A reported gap is progress;
   a guessed method name is a defect.

## AI-Facing Endpoints

{{- if .WithInteraction }}
- `POST /mcp` — MCP JSON-RPC endpoint; the `MCP-Protocol-Version` header selects `2026-07-28` (stateless) or `2025-06-18` (handshake, also selected when the header is absent)
  - `server/discover` — capabilities and supported versions, on `2026-07-28`
  - `initialize` / `notifications/initialized` — handshake, on `2025-06-18` only
  - `ping` — liveness check
  - `tools/list` / `tools/call` — discover and invoke service methods
  - `resources/list` / `resources/read` — read server-exposed data artifacts
  - `resources/templates/list` — discover parameterised resource URI patterns
  - `prompts/list` / `prompts/get` — list and render reusable prompt templates
  - `completion/complete` — auto-complete prompt argument values
  - `logging/setLevel` — adjust server log verbosity
  - On `2026-07-28`: `Mcp-Method` and `Mcp-Name` headers must repeat the method and its target; list results carry `ttlMs` and `cacheScope`; POST is the whole transport
  - On `2025-06-18`: Streamable HTTP with GET for SSE streams and DELETE for session termination
  - Supports MCP Sampling on `2025-06-18`: server can request LLM completions from connected clients
  - Server-initiated notifications: tools/list_changed, prompts/list_changed, resources/list_changed, resources/updated, message, progress
{{- end }}
{{- if .WithOpenAPI }}
- `GET /openapi.json` — generated OpenAPI 3.1 contract
- `GET /schema.json` — generated JSON Schema 2020-12 bundle
- `GET /swagger/` — embedded Swagger UI 5 backed by the generated contract
- `sdk/typescript/client.ts` — generated Fetch-based unary HTTP client
{{- end }}
{{- if .WithConfig }}- `GET /debug/routes` — runtime route inspection when `debug.routes_enabled` is true
{{- end }}
- `GET /health` — liveness and readiness; 503 until the listeners are up and again once shutdown starts
- `GET /livez` — liveness only; 200 while the process is alive
- `GET /readyz` — readiness only; 503 while draining
{{- if .WithOpenAPI }}

## Generate A Frontend From The Contract

The API document is complete enough to build pages from without reading Go
source. Work from the contract, in this order:

1. **Operations** come from `GET /openapi.json`: every route is a path with an
   `operationId` (`<Service>_<Method>`), a `summary`, and request/response
   bodies that are `$ref`s into `components.schemas`.
2. **Message shapes** come from `GET /schema.json`: the same schemas under
   `$defs`, reusable across pages. A field carries its `description` (from the
   IDL doc comment), `type` and `format` (`int64`, `date-time`, `uuid` — map
   them to the right input control), `example`, and the object's `required`
   list. `additionalProperties: false` means render exactly the declared
   fields, no more.
3. **Calls** go through `sdk/typescript/client.ts`: import `APIClient`, one
   instance per base URL, one property per service, one typed method per
   operation. Non-2xx answers throw `APIError` carrying the upstream status
   and body — surface it, never swallow it. Plain `fetch` against the
   documented routes is equally valid.
4. **Route prefix**: every documented path already includes the service
   prefix; call them as documented.

A page set for one entity follows the same shape every time: a list page from
the `List`/`Get` operations, a form from the `Create`/`Update` request schema
(`required` drives validation, `format` drives input types), and delete
confirmation from the `Delete` operation. Never hand-edit
`sdk/typescript/client.ts` — it is regenerated from the same contract; if an
operation you need is missing, stop and report `MICROGEN_API_GAP` instead of
guessing a method name.
{{- end }}

## Common Modifications

1. **Inspect project capabilities or generated ownership** → read `.microgen/manifest.json`
2. **Add business logic** → edit `service/<name>/service.go`
3. **Add endpoint middleware** → edit `endpoint/<name>/custom_chain.go`
4. **Add a new service or model** → run `microgen extend -check -out .` first, then use `-append-service` or `-append-model`
5. **Change AI tool behavior** → the tools are auto-registered from endpoints; change the underlying service logic instead

